## Speculators and the DFlash checkpoint

Sources:

- [vllm-project/speculators at
  `60cd9833fdd1af767001f87423ca49cc41552931`](https://github.com/vllm-project/speculators/tree/60cd9833fdd1af767001f87423ca49cc41552931)
- [RedHatAI/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-speculator.dflash at
  `e44fc94ceb1e7ed45550d15e782aeadd08050483`](https://huggingface.co/RedHatAI/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-speculator.dflash/tree/e44fc94ceb1e7ed45550d15e782aeadd08050483)

The pinned Speculators `pyproject.toml` declares `Apache-2.0` and identifies
Red Hat as the author. That revision carries the Apache License 2.0 and no
`NOTICE` file. The complete terms are in `LICENSE-APACHE-2.0`.

The pinned checkpoint revision identifies a DFlash model trained with
Speculators. It carries no license or notice file. MoEspresso does not
redistribute the checkpoint weights.

Mapped material:

- `src/moespresso/runtime/deepseek_v4/dflash_model.py` is an MLX
  reimplementation of the model, attention, and configuration contracts in
  `src/speculators/models/dflash/`, specialized for the pinned checkpoint and
  MoEspresso's served cache interface.
- `src/moespresso/package/deepseek_v4/dflash_sidecar.py` and
  `src/moespresso/runtime/deepseek_v4/dflash_load.py` implement the pinned
  checkpoint's configuration, tensor-name, and vocabulary-table contracts.

The MoEspresso implementation replaces the PyTorch training graph with an MLX
inference graph, adds persistent windowed context caches, and packages the
checkpoint tensors in a content-hashed sidecar.

## KVarN

Source: [huawei-csl/KVarN at
`7586257f1c632e63187bfacbbe21ccb51540f7b3`](https://github.com/huawei-csl/KVarN/tree/7586257f1c632e63187bfacbbe21ccb51540f7b3).

The pinned repository carries the Apache License 2.0 and no `NOTICE` file. The
complete terms are in `LICENSE-APACHE-2.0`.

Mapped material:

- `src/moespresso/correctness/qwen4/kvarn_reference.py` adapts the normalized
  Hadamard rotation, alternating variance normalization, asymmetric rounding,
  scale absorption, and selected-row reconstruction used by the KVarN K/V
  cache codec.
- `src/moespresso/runtime/qwen4/kvarn_layout.py` records the corresponding
  packed K4/V4 field sizes and metadata classes for released Qwen sparse
  attention.
- `src/moespresso/runtime/qwen4/kvarn_encode.py` encodes a completed released-
  shape K/V tile into that record with MLX operations.
- `src/moespresso/runtime/qwen4/kvarn_selected_rows.py` implements selected-row
  reconstruction from that packed record for Apple Metal.

MoEspresso fixes the codec to the released two-head, 256-wide QSA geometry,
stores K and V codes token-major for sparse selected-row reads, removes vLLM
allocator padding, and keeps the QSA index cache outside the quantized record.
The modified correctness, MLX encoder, and Metal decoder files carry local
modification notices.

